quran[3]{c,v,t}:
  4,176,"They ask you (Esteemed Prophet) for a ruling. Say: ‘Allah gives you a ruling regarding (the inheritance of) the one without a direct heir (kalala). If a man dies, having no children (or parents) but has a sister, she will inherit one-half of what he leaves, whereas her brother will inherit all that she leaves if she has left no children behind. If there are two sisters, then they shall receive two-thirds of what he leaves. But if there are (several) brothers and sisters, then the male’s share shall be equal to the share of two females. Allah explains (the laws) for you, lest you go astray. Allah is All-knowing of everything.’"
  5,1,"O believers! Fulfil (your) promises. All grazing livestock are permitted to you, except what is (now) announced to you, disallowing the hunting of game while you are in pilgrim sanctity. Indeed, Allah decrees whatever He wills."
  5,2,"O believers! Do not violate Allah’s sacraments (i.e. the sacred signs and rituals of the pilgrimage), neither (the sanctity of) the sacred month nor the sacrificial offering, nor the necklaces (hung around the necks of the sacrificial animals), nor those going to the Sacred House seeking the grace and pleasure of their Lord. And when you become free from the (obligation of) pilgrim sanctity, you may hunt for game. And do not let your hatred for a people who (once) turned you away from the Sacred Mosque lead you to commit aggression. And help one another in righteousness and God-vigilance (guarding yourselves against evil), and do not cooperate in sin and aggression. And be God-conscious. Indeed, Allah is severe in retribution."
